    <problem>
      <p>$$y^{''} + 4y^{\prime} + 6y = 0,$$ $$y(0) = 0,$$ $$y^{\prime}(0) = \sqrt{2}$$</p>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <p>$$y = e^{-2x}\text{sin}\mspace{2mu}\left( {\sqrt{2}x} \right)$$</p>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
